<h2>Best Alternatives to the FitDesk</h2>
<h3>If you want to keep your own desk: DeskCycle Ellipse</h3>
<p>The [[amazon:deskcycle-ellipse|DeskCycle Ellipse]] is a low-profile seated elliptical with a wide resistance range. It is the closest under desk option to the FitDesk's effort level, and it fits under most standard desks. Read our <a href="/deskcycle-ellipse-review/">DeskCycle Ellipse review</a>.</p>
<h3>If you want the quietest all-day option: Cubii JR2</h3>
<p>The [[amazon:cubii-jr2|Cubii JR2]] is compact and whisper quiet, designed for steady light movement through the workday. See our guide to <a href="/cubii-under-desk-elliptical-is-it-really-worth-using-every-day/">using a Cubii every day</a>.</p>
<h3>If you prefer a bike motion under your desk: DeskCycle 2</h3>
<p>The [[amazon:deskcycle-2|DeskCycle 2]] gives you the cycling feel without a separate seat or desk, and its low profile suits standard desks.</p>
